* sg13g2-bandgap -- bandgap_trim ladder range/resolution/linearity
* coverage bench (issue #229 -- AC1 evidence for DR-0011's Trim row).
* Generated from testbench/tb_trim_coverage.spice.tmpl by
* sim/trim-coverage/run_trim_coverage.sh -- do not edit a generated
* netlist-snapshots/*.spice file directly, edit this template and re-run.
*
* Generated for: point=sf temp=27C vdd=3.30V
* trim_code=255
* DUT git sha: core=9530863 trim=9530863 amp=397fe2d startup=66ac99d seeds=20260830-132425-d83f7c4.csv@94207b4
* PDK: ihp-sg13g2 /Users/rwalters/share/pdk (see sim/pdk.json for the pinned release)
* OSDI models: /Users/rwalters/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi (built by sim/tools/build-osdi.sh)
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------- method
* The SAME co-simulated closed-loop topology every sim/closed-loop-*
* experiment in this tree uses (core + amp + startup, loop NOT broken).
* One .op per netlist at ONE trim code; the driver renders one netlist
* per (corner, supply, code) via sed -- the ONLY per-point difference is
* the subcircuit-local .param trim_code above. The strap resistors inside
* bandgap_trim decode trim_code into closed/open links (see
* design/bandgap_trim.sch), so vref(code) is measured through the real
* ladder, never through a synthetic voltage source.
*
* vref = VBE(Q3) + I*(R1 + Rtrim) with I set entirely by the R2/Q1/Q2
* loop (independent of the output branch), so vref is linear in
* trim_code to first order -- the driver VERIFIES that per corner from
* this run's own codes {0,1,2,4,...,128,129,255} rather than assuming
* it: single-bit codes give each group's measured weight (must equal
* 2^b LSBs), code 129 gives the direct step, code 255 the full-scale
* linearity residual (see run_trim_coverage.sh's analysis block).
.nodeset v(fb)=2.52426e+00 v(sns1)=7.08222e-01 v(sns2)=7.08155e-01 v(vref)=1.04975e+00

.lib "/Users/rwalters/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerHBT.lib" hbt_typ
.lib "/Users/rwalters/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib" mos_sf
.lib "/Users/rwalters/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib" res_typ

.options temp=27 tnom=27

* FIXTURE -- vdd is a fixed DC source: this bench measures the settled DC
* operating point per code, not a startup transient.
Vvdd vdd 0 dc 3.30
Vvss vss 0 dc 0
Vsub sub! vss dc 0

* DUT -- design/netlist/bandgap_core.spice, verbatim (R1 base l=37.2u
* to node tn0 + XXTRIM bandgap_trim tn0->cb3, per issue #229 -- see
* design/bandgap_trim_network.md), with the trim ladder subcircuit
* definition copied verbatim from design/netlist/bandgap_trim.spice
* (its subcircuit-local .param trim_code carries THIS point's code).
XM1 sns1 fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XQ1 sns1 sns1 vss vss npn13G2 Nx=1
XM2A sns2 fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=9u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XM2B sns2 fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=1u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XR2 sns2 cb2 sub! rppd w=2u l=82.7u m=1 b=0
XQ2 cb2 cb2 vss vss npn13G2 Nx=8
XM3A vref fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=8u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XM3B vref fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=1u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XM3C vref fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=1u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XR1 vref tn0 sub! rppd w=2u l=37.2u m=1 b=0
XXTRIM tn0 cb3 sub! bandgap_trim
XQ3 cb3 cb3 vss vss npn13G2 Nx=1

.subckt bandgap_trim in out sub
*.iopin in
*.iopin out
*.iopin sub
XRU1 in t001 sub rppd w=2u l=3.43u m=1 b=0
